    <report type:"WARNING">
      description : "1.14 WN10-00-000060"
      info        : "Non system-created file shares on a system must limit access to groups that require it.

GROUP ID: V-220710RULE ID: SV-220710r958524

Shares which provide network access, should not typically exist on a workstation except for system-created administrative shares, and could potentially expose sensitive information. If a share is necessary, share permissions, as well as NTFS permissions, must be reconfigured to give the minimum access to those accounts that require it.

NOTE: Nessus has not performed this check. Please review the benchmark to ensure target compliance."
      solution    : "If a non system-created share is required on a system, configure the share and NTFS permissions to limit access to the specific groups or accounts that require it.

Remove any unnecessary non-system created shares."
      reference   : "800-171|3.13.4,800-171r3|03.13.04,800-53|SC-4,800-53r5|SC-4,CCI|CCI-001090,CSF2.0|PR.DS-01,CSF2.0|PR.DS-02,CSF2.0|PR.DS-10,CSF2.0|PR.IR-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ITSG-33|SC-4,ITSG-33|SC-4a.,LEVEL|2M,Rule-ID|SV-220710r958524_rule,STIG-ID|WN10-00-000060,Vuln-ID|V-220710"
