    </if>

    <if>
      <condition type:"AND">
        <custom_item>
          type        : REGISTRY_SETTING
          description : "Windows 10 LTSC\B"
          value_type  : POLICY_TEXT
          value_data  : "^Windows 10.*LTS[CB]$"
          reg_key     : "HKLM\Software\Microsoft\Windows Nt\Currentversion"
          reg_item    : "ProductName"
          check_type  : CHECK_REGEX
        </custom_item>

        <custom_item>
          type        : REGISTRY_SETTING
          description : "Windows 10 LTSC\B 1507 and 1607."
          value_type  : POLICY_TEXT
          value_data  : "^(10240|14393)$"
          reg_key     : "HKLM\Software\Microsoft\Windows Nt\Currentversion"
          reg_item    : "CurrentBuildNumber"
          check_type  : CHECK_REGEX
        </custom_item>
      </condition>

      <then>
        <report type:"PASSED">
          description : "1.153 WN10-CC-000252"
          info        : "Windows 10 must be configured to disable Windows Game Recording and Broadcasting.

GROUP ID: V-220845RULE ID: SV-220845r958478

Windows Game Recording and Broadcasting is intended for use with games, however it could potentially record screen shots of other applications and expose sensitive data. Disabling the feature will prevent this from occurring."
          solution    : 'Configure the policy value for

Computer Configuration >> Administrative Templates >> Windows Components >> Windows Game Recording and Broadcasting >> \'Enables or disables Windows Game Recording and Broadcasting\'

to \'Disabled\'.'
          reference   : "800-171|3.4.6,800-171|3.4.7,800-171r3|03.04.06,800-171r3|03.04.06a.,800-53|CM-7,800-53|CM-7a.,800-53r5|CM-7a.,CCI|CCI-000381,CN-L3|7.1.3.5(c),CN-L3|8.1.4.4(a),CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF|PR.PT-3,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ITSG-33|CM-7,ITSG-33|CM-7a.,LEVEL|2M,NIAv2|SS15a,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|2.2.1,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|2.2.2,PCI-DSSv4.0|2.2.3,QCSC-v1|3.2,Rule-ID|SV-220845r958478_rule,STIG-ID|WN10-CC-000252,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3,Vuln-ID|V-220845"
