    <custom_item>
      type         : SERVICE_POLICY
      description  : "1.37 WN10-00-000175"
      info         : "The Secondary Logon service must be disabled on Windows 10.

GROUP ID: V-220732RULE ID: SV-220732r958478

The Secondary Logon service provides a means for entering alternate credentials, typically used to run commands with elevated privileges. Using privileged credentials in a standard user session can expose those credentials to theft."
      solution     : 'Configure the \'Secondary Logon\' service \'Startup Type\' to \'Disabled\'.'
      reference    : "800-171|3.4.6,800-171|3.4.7,800-171r3|03.04.06,800-171r3|03.04.06a.,800-53|CM-7,800-53|CM-7a.,800-53r5|CM-7a.,CCI|CCI-000381,CN-L3|7.1.3.5(c),CN-L3|8.1.4.4(a),CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF|PR.PT-3,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ITSG-33|CM-7,ITSG-33|CM-7a.,LEVEL|2M,NIAv2|SS15a,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|2.2.1,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|2.2.2,PCI-DSSv4.0|2.2.3,QCSC-v1|3.2,Rule-ID|SV-220732r958478_rule,STIG-ID|WN10-00-000175,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3,Vuln-ID|V-220732"
      see_also     : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/23869"
      value_type   : SERVICE_SET
      value_data   : "Disabled"
      service_name : "seclogon"
    </custom_item>

    <report type:"WARNING">
      description : "1.38 WN10-00-000190"
      info        : "Orphaned security identifiers (SIDs) must be removed from user rights on Windows 10.

GROUP ID: V-220733RULE ID: SV-220733r991589

Accounts or groups given rights on a system may show up as unresolved SIDs for various reasons including deletion of the accounts or groups. If the account or group objects are reanimated, there is a potential they may still have rights no longer intended. Valid domain accounts or groups may also show up as unresolved SIDs if a connection to the domain cannot be established for some reason.

NOTE: Nessus has not performed this check. Please review the benchmark to ensure target compliance."
      solution    : "Remove any unresolved SIDs found in User Rights assignments and determined to not be for currently valid accounts or groups by removing the accounts or groups from the appropriate group policy."
      reference   : "800-171|3.4.2,800-171r3|03.04.02a.,800-53|CM-6b.,800-53r5|CM-6b.,CCI|CCI-000366,CN-L3|8.1.10.6(d),CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF2.0|DE.CM-09,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ISO-27001-2022|A.8.9,ITSG-33|CM-6b.,LEVEL|2M,NESA|T3.2.1,Rule-ID|SV-220733r991589_rule,STIG-ID|WN10-00-000190,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3,Vuln-ID|V-220733"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/23869"
    </report>

    <custom_item>
      type            : AUDIT_POWERSHELL
      description     : "1.39 WN10-00-000210"
      info            : "Bluetooth must be turned off unless approved by the organization.

GROUP ID: V-220734RULE ID: SV-220734r958478

If not configured properly, Bluetooth may allow rogue devices to communicate with a system. If a rogue device is paired with a system, there is potential for sensitive information to be compromised."
      solution        : "Turn off Bluetooth radios not organizationally approved. Establish an organizational policy for the use of Bluetooth."
      reference       : "800-171|3.4.6,800-171|3.4.7,800-171r3|03.04.06,800-171r3|03.04.06a.,800-53|CM-7,800-53|CM-7a.,800-53r5|CM-7a.,CCI|CCI-000381,CN-L3|7.1.3.5(c),CN-L3|8.1.4.4(a),CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF|PR.PT-3,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ITSG-33|CM-7,ITSG-33|CM-7a.,LEVEL|2M,NIAv2|SS15a,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|2.2.1,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|2.2.2,PCI-DSSv4.0|2.2.3,QCSC-v1|3.2,Rule-ID|SV-220734r958478_rule,STIG-ID|WN10-00-000210,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3,Vuln-ID|V-220734"
      see_also        : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/23869"
      value_type      : POLICY_TEXT
      value_data      : "Status.+:[ ]([Dd]own)|No entries found"
      powershell_args : "$output=(Get-NetAdapter | Where-Object {$_.Name -match 'Bluetooth'} | Format-List Status,Name,InterfaceDescription,AdminStatus); if ([string]::IsNullOrEmpty($output)) { 'No entries found' } else { $output };"
      check_type      : CHECK_REGEX
    </custom_item>

    <custom_item>
      type            : AUDIT_POWERSHELL
      description     : "1.40 WN10-00-000220"
      info            : "Bluetooth must be turned off when not in use.

GROUP ID: V-220735RULE ID: SV-220735r958478

If not configured properly, Bluetooth may allow rogue devices to communicate with a system. If a rogue device is paired with a system, there is potential for sensitive information to be compromised."
      solution        : "Turn off Bluetooth radios when not in use. Establish an organizational policy for the use of Bluetooth to include training of personnel."
