      reg_item             : "AcceptIncomingRequests"
      reg_ignore_hku_users : "S-1-5-18,S-1-5-19,S-1-5-20"
      severity             : MEDIUM
    </custom_item>

    <report type:"WARNING">
      description : "1.43 WN10-00-000250"
      info        : "Windows 10 nonpersistent VM sessions must not exceed 24 hours.

GROUP ID: V-220738RULE ID: SV-220738r958552

For virtual desktop implementations (VDIs) where the virtual desktop instance is deleted or refreshed upon logoff, the organization should enforce that sessions be terminated within 24 hours. This would ensure any data stored on the VM that is not encrypted or covered by Credential Guard is deleted.

NOTE: Nessus has not performed this check. Please review the benchmark to ensure target compliance."
      solution    : "Set nonpersistent VM sessions to not exceed 24 hours."
      reference   : "800-171|3.13.16,800-171r3|03.13.08,800-53|SC-28,800-53r5|SC-28,CCI|CCI-001199,CN-L3|8.1.4.7(b),CN-L3|8.1.4.8(b),CSF|PR.DS-1,CSF2.0|PR.DS-01,GDPR|32.1.a,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),HIPAA|164.312(a)(2)(iv),HIPAA|164.312(e)(2)(ii),ISO-27001-2022|A.5.10,ISO-27001-2022|A.5.33,ITSG-33|SC-28,ITSG-33|SC-28a.,LEVEL|2M,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|3.4,PCI-DSSv4.0|3.3.2,PCI-DSSv4.0|3.5.1,QCSC-v1|5.2.2,QCSC-v1|6.2,Rule-ID|SV-220738r958552_rule,STIG-ID|WN10-00-000250,Vuln-ID|V-220738"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/23869"
    </report>

    <if>
      <condition type:"AND">
        <custom_item>
          type            : AUDIT_POWERSHELL
          description     : "System is a member of a domain"
          value_type      : POLICY_TEXT
          value_data      : "True"
          powershell_args : "(Get-WmiObject -Class Win32_ComputerSystem).PartOfDomain"
        </custom_item>
      </condition>

      <then>
        <if>
          <condition auto:"FAILED" type:"AND">
            <custom_item>
              type        : REG_CHECK
              description : "PortProxy"
              value_type  : POLICY_TEXT
              value_data  : "HKLM\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Services\PortProxy\v4tov4\tcp"
              reg_option  : MUST_NOT_EXIST
            </custom_item>

            <custom_item>
              type            : AUDIT_POWERSHELL
              description     : "netsh"
              value_type      : POLICY_TEXT
              value_data      : "Not found"
              powershell_args : "$output=(netsh interface portproxy show all); foreach-object { if($output){ $result='Proxied ports found' } else { $result='Not found' }; $result };"
              check_type      : CHECK_REGEX
            </custom_item>
          </condition>

          <then>
            <report type:"PASSED">
              description : "1.44 WN10-00-000395"
              info        : "Windows 10 must not have portproxy enabled or in use.

GROUP ID: V-257593RULE ID: SV-257593r991589

Having portproxy enabled or configured in Windows 10 could allow a man-in-the-middle attack."
              solution    : 'Contact the Administrator to run \'netsh interface portproxy delete\' with elevation. Remove any enabled portproxies that may be configured.'
              reference   : "800-171|3.4.6,800-171|3.4.7,800-171r3|03.04.06,800-171r3|03.04.06a.,800-53|CM-7,800-53|CM-7a.,800-53r5|CM-7a.,CCI|CCI-000381,CN-L3|7.1.3.5(c),CN-L3|8.1.4.4(a),CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF|PR.PT-3,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ITSG-33|CM-7,ITSG-33|CM-7a.,LEVEL|2M,NIAv2|SS15a,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|2.2.1,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|2.2.2,PCI-DSSv4.0|2.2.3,QCSC-v1|3.2,Rule-ID|SV-257593r991589_rule,STIG-ID|WN10-00-000395,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3,Vuln-ID|V-257593"
              see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/23869"
              show_output : YES
            </report>
          </then>
        </if>
      </then>

      <else>
        <report type:"PASSED">
          description : "1.44 WN10-00-000395"
          info        : "Windows 10 must not have portproxy enabled or in use.

GROUP ID: V-257593RULE ID: SV-257593r991589

Having portproxy enabled or configured in Windows 10 could allow a man-in-the-middle attack."
          solution    : 'Contact the Administrator to run \'netsh interface portproxy delete\' with elevation. Remove any enabled portproxies that may be configured.'
          reference   : "800-171|3.4.6,800-171|3.4.7,800-171r3|03.04.06,800-171r3|03.04.06a.,800-53|CM-7,800-53|CM-7a.,800-53r5|CM-7a.,CCI|CCI-000381,CN-L3|7.1.3.5(c),CN-L3|8.1.4.4(a),CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF|PR.PT-3,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ITSG-33|CM-7,ITSG-33|CM-7a.,LEVEL|2M,NIAv2|SS15a,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|2.2.1,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|2.2.2,PCI-DSSv4.0|2.2.3,QCSC-v1|3.2,Rule-ID|SV-257593r991589_rule,STIG-ID|WN10-00-000395,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3,Vuln-ID|V-257593"
