    <if>
      <condition type:"AND">
        <custom_item>
          type            : AUDIT_POWERSHELL
          description     : "Test the Lockout Threshold"
          value_type      : POLICY_TEXT
          value_data      : "[Ll]ockout threshold:[\s]*[1-9][\d]*"
          powershell_args : "net accounts | findstr /c:'Lockout threshold'"
          check_type      : CHECK_REGEX
        </custom_item>
      </condition>

      <then>
        <custom_item>
          type           : LOCKOUT_POLICY
          description    : "1.45 WN10-AC-000005"
          info           : "Windows 10 account lockout duration must be configured to 15 minutes or greater.

GROUP ID: V-220739RULE ID: SV-220739r958736

The account lockout feature, when enabled, prevents brute-force password attacks on the system. This parameter specifies the amount of time that an account will remain locked after the specified number of failed logon attempts."
          solution       : 'Configure the policy value for

Computer Configuration >> Windows Settings >> Security Settings >> Account Policies >> Account Lockout Policy >> \'Account lockout duration\'

to \'15\' minutes or greater.

A value of \'0\' is also acceptable, requiring an administrator to unlock the account.'
          reference      : "800-171|3.1.8,800-171r3|03.01.08b.,800-53|AC-7b.,800-53r5|AC-7b.,CCI|CCI-002238,CN-L3|7.1.2.7(f),CN-L3|7.1.3.1(c),CSF2.0|PR.AA-03,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ISO-27001-2022|A.8.5,ITSG-33|AC-7b.,LEVEL|2M,NESA|T5.5.1,NIAv2|AM24,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|8.1.7,PCI-DSSv4.0|8.3.4,Rule-ID|SV-220739r958736_rule,STIG-ID|WN10-AC-000005,TBA-FIISB|36.2.4,TBA-FIISB|45.1.2,Vuln-ID|V-220739"
          see_also       : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/23869"
          value_type     : TIME_MINUTE
          value_data     : "[15..MAX]" || "0"
          lockout_policy : LOCKOUT_DURATION
        </custom_item>
      </then>

      <else>
