    <if>
      <condition type:"AND">
        <custom_item>
          type            : AUDIT_POWERSHELL
          description     : "Test the Lockout Threshold"
          value_type      : POLICY_TEXT
          value_data      : "[Ll]ockout threshold:[\s]*[1-9][\d]*"
          powershell_args : "net accounts | findstr /c:'Lockout threshold'"
          check_type      : CHECK_REGEX
        </custom_item>
      </condition>

      <then>
        <custom_item>
          type           : LOCKOUT_POLICY
          description    : "1.46 WN10-AC-000010"
          info           : "The number of allowed bad logon attempts must be configured to 3 or less.

GROUP ID: V-220740RULE ID: SV-220740r958388

The account lockout feature, when enabled, prevents brute-force password attacks on the system. The higher this value is, the less effective the account lockout feature will be in protecting the local system. The number of bad logon attempts must be reasonably small to minimize the possibility of a successful password attack, while allowing for honest errors made during a normal user logon."
          solution       : 'Configure the policy value for

Computer Configuration >> Windows Settings >> Security Settings >> Account Policies >> Account Lockout Policy >> \'Account lockout threshold\'

to \'3\' or less invalid logon attempts (excluding \'0\' which is unacceptable).'
          reference      : "800-171|3.1.8,800-171r3|03.01.08a.,800-53|AC-7a.,800-53r5|AC-7a.,CCI|CCI-000044,CN-L3|8.1.4.1(b),CSF2.0|PR.AA-03,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ISO-27001-2022|A.8.5,ITSG-33|AC-7a.,LEVEL|2M,NESA|T5.5.1,NIAv2|AM24,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|8.1.6,PCI-DSSv4.0|8.3.4,Rule-ID|SV-220740r958388_rule,STIG-ID|WN10-AC-000010,TBA-FIISB|45.1.2,TBA-FIISB|45.2.1,TBA-FIISB|45.2.2,Vuln-ID|V-220740"
          see_also       : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/23869"
          value_type     : TIME_MINUTE
          value_data     : "[1..3]"
          lockout_policy : LOCKOUT_THRESHOLD
        </custom_item>
      </then>

      <else>
        <report type:"FAILED">
          description : "1.46 WN10-AC-000010"
          info        : "The number of allowed bad logon attempts must be configured to 3 or less.

GROUP ID: V-220740RULE ID: SV-220740r958388

The account lockout feature, when enabled, prevents brute-force password attacks on the system. The higher this value is, the less effective the account lockout feature will be in protecting the local system. The number of bad logon attempts must be reasonably small to minimize the possibility of a successful password attack, while allowing for honest errors made during a normal user logon."
          solution    : 'Configure the policy value for

Computer Configuration >> Windows Settings >> Security Settings >> Account Policies >> Account Lockout Policy >> \'Account lockout threshold\'

to \'3\' or less invalid logon attempts (excluding \'0\' which is unacceptable).'
          reference   : "800-171|3.1.8,800-171r3|03.01.08a.,800-53|AC-7a.,800-53r5|AC-7a.,CCI|CCI-000044,CN-L3|8.1.4.1(b),CSF2.0|PR.AA-03,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ISO-27001-2022|A.8.5,ITSG-33|AC-7a.,LEVEL|2M,NESA|T5.5.1,NIAv2|AM24,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|8.1.6,PCI-DSSv4.0|8.3.4,Rule-ID|SV-220740r958388_rule,STIG-ID|WN10-AC-000010,TBA-FIISB|45.1.2,TBA-FIISB|45.2.1,TBA-FIISB|45.2.2,Vuln-ID|V-220740"
